{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 40 '\\\\bD693\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -62; rg -n 'maximum|context|input_tokens|gpt-6-luna' src/hivemind/model.py poc/config/poc-v119.json | head -23\"","aggregated_output":"10414:## D693 · 2026-11-21 · Under Alex's A (D691): the design for linking related questions reaches council consensus at $0; three choices go to Alex before any build or send; the self-made reference is traced\n10415-\n10416-- **Source of authority:** Alex's \"A\" (D691) and D692's registered next step (\"the dependency design review reopens at $0 ... then goes\n10417-  to Alex before any build or send\"); Alex, 2026-11-21: \"好继续\".\n10418-- **Council R** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/RESULT.md`; Codex thread `01a1fcdb…`, rounds 1–3;\n10419-  round 2 DISAGREE with five changes, round 3 DISAGREE on one, all taken; consensus): for the product (poc-v118, no seed edges) a\n10420-  build-ready design is reachable after Alex's choices and a $0 proof. The matching step chooses links (D51, D368 item 2) through one\n10421-  three-way matcher question that also covers an existing question reading a newly opened one (D191 point 2 at opening; old-2 opens\n10422-  Data Center before total revenue); a link between two already open questions stays a separate slice. The matcher answers the\n10423-  relation's sign and code maps the label from typed rung bounds. The reader is shown the read judgement's comparison point and its\n10424-  forecast in full, labelled as the system's, beside a bounded reasons excerpt. A chosen link moves no statement (106 items linked to\n10425-  both questions in old-2 are exposed to literal D265). D542's five items are settled for the product as written in the record.\n10426-- **Withdrawn by Claude in round 1:** a link written by code from typed keys (a hand list over measure names, D167, AGENTS §2). Corrected\n10427-  by Codex in round 2: July already holds an outside total-revenue estimate (Bloomberg-compiled $393B, e195), so July alone is the first\n10428-  send. Corrected in round 3: both questions are judged fresh in every sequence.\n10429-- **The self-made reference** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md`, `reference_census.py`, $0): 44 of\n10430-  2,375 number judgements (1.9%) present the system's own earlier figure as the reference, 33 of them on the FY2027 Data Center question\n10431-  (old-1, old-2); mechanism traced on old-2 v9 07-06 to 09-20: the previous conclusion is shown as rung and reasons only, without the\n10432-  source of its figures, and no sentence of judging-v7 covers \"no market figure supplied\"; the Wall Street estimate sits under total\n10433-  revenue only. Its own fix (a sourced reference) returns to Alex separately, after the link is measured.\n10434-- **Decided (council consensus; Alex's choices pending):** nothing is built or sent. To Alex: (a) a chosen reading link leaves filing\n10435-  alone; (b) open new matching and judging versions for the shared mechanism, the first test accepting only the existing-reader /\n10436-  new-target case; (c) after the $0 proof passes the council, the July comparison (old-2, 07-10 to 07-12, three linked and three\n10437-  control sequences, both questions fresh, pass rule in `codex-r2.md` §7(b)), cap $0.15, estimate $0.06–0.07. Recommendation: all three.\n10438-\n10439-## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10440-\n10441:- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21), replying to the three choices of D693: \"A\". The options were:\n10442-  - **A**, recommended: (a) a chosen reading link leaves evidence filing alone (D265 applies only to a stated hierarchy); (b) open new\n10443-    matching and judging versions for the shared mechanism (both opening orders; the first test accepts only the existing-reader /\n10444-    new-target case); (c) after the $0 proof has passed the council, the July comparison (old-2, 07-10 to 07-12, three linked and three\n10445-    control sequences, both questions fresh, pass rule `dependency-design/codex-r2.md` §7(b)), cap $0.15, estimate $0.06–0.07;\n10446-  - **B**, the code and the $0 proof only, asking again before the paid test;\n10447-  - **C**, not now.\n10448-- **Decided (Alex):** A. poc-v118 stays the product and the control; the linking version is a new configuration. The sourced-reference\n10449:  change is not opened (it returns after the July measurement, D693).\n10450:- **Next:** the $0 work of D693 in order (tables and request audit; the July control rebuilt by request identity and filing replayed;\n10451-  real checks and writer with fixed answers for both orders and the listed events; built requests inspected, rule frozen, cap set),\n10452-  then the council on the proof, then the send.\n10453-\n10454-## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n10455-\n10456-- **The question** (after council R round 4, `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r4.md`, NOT READY: the\n10457-  design's blanket exclusion of theme links narrowed the agreed lifecycle, and the full scope — themes shown once with the link's\n10458-  direction, a theme reading an asset, closed events read as historical until a successor, two questions opened by one article — needs\n10459-  more design rounds): \"连题的第一版，范围要多大？\" Options: only number questions (recommended): link two five-rung number questions\n10460-  of the asset kind, one of them newly opened; themes already reach every asset question through the theme block (D191, D195);\n10461-  yes/no event questions and two questions opened by the same article wait for a later version. Or the agreed design in full.\n10462-- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"只连数字题 (推荐)\".\n10463-- **Decided (Alex):** the first linking version links only a newly opened number question and an open number question it was shown,\n10464-  in either reading direction (both five-rung asset ladders with typed bounds). No theme, event or same-article pair is linked in this\n10465-  version; each is a later version Alex opens. D694 otherwise stands.\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:8:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:14:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:20:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:26:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:32:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:38:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:44:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:50:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:56:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:62:      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:76:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:82:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:88:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\npoc/config/poc-v119.json:94:    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:32:# gpt-6-luna: the published standard rates on 2026-10-25 (developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna: $0.10/M input, $0.50/M output,\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:35:PRICES = {'gpt-6-luna': (0.10, 0.50), 'gpt-6.1-sol': (2.00, 10.00), 'gpt-6-astra': (10.00, 50.00), 'claude-opus-5-5': (4.00, 20.00), 'deepseek-flash': (0.30, 1.20), 'deepseek-v4-pro': (1.32, 3.96),\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:37:CACHED_INPUT_SHARE = 0.10          # cached input tokens are priced at 10% of the input rate (gpt-6-luna page, read again 2026-10-27)\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:43:  input_tokens integer, output_tokens integer, cost_usd real, seconds real, created_at text\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:64:    input_tokens: int\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:81:            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:105:            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:258:        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:259:        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/store.py | sed -n '24,145p'; rg -n 'run\\\\(|jev-links|matching.engine' src/hivemind/parallel_day.py scripts/replay.py\"","aggregated_output":"    24\t    'same_claims': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer',                    # D204: the matcher read the new piece as the same claim as the old; both stored, both in force\n    25\t    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer, kind text default \\'\\'',   # kind: '' (a seed's or the generative matcher's row, read as before) or 'reads' (a chosen reading link, D694)\n    26\t    'dependency_resolutions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer',\n    27\t    'successions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer',\n    28\t    'handovers': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text',\n    29\t    'match_records': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text',\n    30\t    'processing_steps': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text',\n    31\t    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\n    32\t    'late_statements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer',\n    33\t    'days_completed': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text',\n    34\t    # D694: how the links of an article were chosen (views/links.py), append-only per attempt: proposed, then committed or failed\n    35\t    'link_selections': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, attempt_id text, seq integer, input_id text, config_checksum text, status text, record_json text',\n    36\t    # D149 research groups: an ongoing business subject several distinct theses belong to; membership is decided by extraction and written with the thesis\n    37\t    'thesis_groups': 'group_id text primary key, name text, scope text, aliases text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\n    38\t    'thesis_group_members': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, basis text',\n    39\t    # D166 (2026-11-01): the names a later declaration gives a stored group, appended once each; a group's aliases are its creation's plus these\n    40\t    'thesis_group_aliases': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, alias text, seq integer, input_id text',\n    41\t}\n    42\t\n    43\tINDEXES = [\n    44\t    'create index if not exists views_object on views(object_id)',\n    45\t    'create index if not exists judgements_view on judgements(view_id, judgement_id)',\n    46\t    # 06-views step 7: a view is judged once per round (one item = one sequence number)\n    47\t    'create unique index if not exists judgements_once_per_round on judgements(view_id, seq)',\n    48\t    'create index if not exists links_view on evidence_links(view_id)',\n    49\t    'create index if not exists links_evidence on evidence_links(evidence_id)',\n    50\t    'create index if not exists sources_evidence on evidence_sources(evidence_id)',\n    51\t    'create index if not exists steps_input on processing_steps(input_id, id)',\n    52\t    'create index if not exists switches_view on view_switches(view_id, id)',\n    53\t    'create index if not exists deps_view on dependencies(view_id)',\n    54\t]\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef open_db(path):\n    58\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    59\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\n    60\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    61\t    for name, columns in TABLES.items():\n    62\t        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({columns})')\n    63\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n    64\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n    65\t    for statement in INDEXES:\n    66\t        conn.execute(statement)\n    67\t    ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n    68\t    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    69\t    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    70\t    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\n    71\t    conn.commit()\n    72\t    return conn\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\tdef insert(conn, table, **fields):\n    76\t    columns = list(fields)\n    77\t    cursor = conn.execute(f'insert into {table} ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})', [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    78\t    return cursor.lastrowid\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t# ---------- views ----------\n    82\t\n    83\tdef create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\n    84\t    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\n    85\t           question=question, due_day=due_day, year=year, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id, created_at=created_at)\n    86\t    for position, rung in enumerate(rungs, start=1):\n    87\t        insert(conn, 'rungs', view_id=view_id, position=position, label=rung['label'], condition=rung['condition'], lo=rung.get('lo'), hi=rung.get('hi'))\n    88\t    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\n    89\t    conn.execute('insert into views_fts (view_id, text) values (?, ?)', (view_id, f'{object_id} {looks_at} {question}'))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tdef view(conn, view_id):\n    93\t    row = conn.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n    94\t    return dict(row) if row else None\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\tdef rungs_of(conn, view_id):\n    98\t    \"\"\"The rungs with their bounds when the ledger has them (keyed views); a ledger written before keys has no lo/hi columns.\"\"\"\n    99\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\n   100\t    has_bounds = any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rows) or view_key(conn, view_id) is not None\n   101\t    return [dict(position=r['position'], label=r['label'], condition=r['condition'],\n   102\t                 **({'lo': r.get('lo'), 'hi': r.get('hi')} if has_bounds else {})) for r in rows]\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\tdef add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\n   106\t    \"\"\"The view's key (keyed-views-plan.md 2.1), written once with the view.\"\"\"\n   107\t    from .. import universe as _universe\n   108\t    from .identity import is_shared\n   109\t    scope_source = 'shared' if is_shared(key) else key.get('scope_source', 'model')      # D197: an aggregate's scope is wording\n   110\t    insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id=view_id, measure=key['measure'], scope=key.get('scope', ''), scope_key=_universe.scope_key(key.get('scope', '')),\n   111\t           period_start=key.get('period_start', ''), period_end=key.get('period_end', ''), basis=key.get('basis', 'n/a'), unit=key.get('unit', 'n/a'),\n   112\t           event_type=key.get('event_type', 'n/a'), seq=seq, scope_source=scope_source, key_version=key.get('key_version'))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\tdef ensure_key_columns(conn):\n   116\t    \"\"\"A keyed ledger written before `scope_source` gains the column (append-only forbids updates, not new columns); its\n   117\t    earlier keys read as model-owned scopes unless the scope is empty.\"\"\"\n   118\t    columns = [r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(view_keys)')]\n   119\t    if columns and 'scope_source' not in columns:\n   120\t        conn.execute('alter table view_keys add column scope_source text')\n   121\t    if columns and 'key_version' not in columns:\n   122\t        conn.execute('alter table view_keys add column key_version integer')\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\tdef ensure_group_tables(conn):\n   126\t    \"\"\"A ledger written before research groups (D165) gains the group tables at its first write; nothing else changes.\"\"\"\n   127\t    for name in ('thesis_groups', 'thesis_group_members', 'thesis_group_aliases'):\n   128\t        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({TABLES[name]})')\n   129\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n   130\t        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n   131\t    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n   132\t    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\n   133\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_groups)')}\n   134\t    if 'aliases' not in columns:\n   135\t        conn.execute('alter table thesis_groups add column aliases text')\n   136\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_group_members)')}\n   137\t    if 'basis' not in columns:\n   138\t        conn.execute('alter table thesis_group_members add column basis text')\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\tdef ensure_writable_columns(conn):\n   142\t    \"\"\"Upgrade columns at a write boundary, including a legacy database restored into an open connection.\"\"\"\n   143\t    ensure_key_columns(conn)\n   144\t    ensure_group_tables(conn)\n   145\t    columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(rungs)')}\nscripts/replay.py:13:Jev matching questions at a time (8; one at a time for another matching engine); the ledger equals the serial one for\nscripts/replay.py:67:    \"\"\"D694: poc-v119's matching engine runs only in its July test harness in this version, not from an ordinary launcher.\"\"\"\nscripts/replay.py:68:    if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev-links':\nscripts/replay.py:69:        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version}: matching engine jev-links is not a product entry point in this version (D694)')\nscripts/replay.py:108:        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\nscripts/replay.py:113:    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\nsrc/hivemind/parallel_day.py:8:workers receive copies and write only the thread-safe call archive. Opt-in through `replay.run(day_runner=...)`;\nsrc/hivemind/parallel_day.py:93:        if cfg.matching.engine not in ('jev', 'jev-links') and self.jev_workers != 1:\nsrc/hivemind/parallel_day.py:159:                result = rounds.run(conn, archive, frozen_cfg, frozen_universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import json, sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hivemind import config, model\np=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite\\\").resolve()\ndb=sqlite3.connect(f\\\"{p.as_uri()}?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\ncfg=config.load(\\\"poc/config/poc-v118.json\\\")\nseen={}\ntarget_rows=0\nlive_targets=0\nfor cid,digest,raw in db.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_sha256,request_json from model_calls where purpose=\\\\x27judge\\\\x27 order by call_id\\\"):\n    request=json.loads(raw)\n    user=request[\\\"messages\\\"][-1][\\\"content\\\"]\n    vs=user.split(\\\" \\\",2)[1] if user.startswith(\\\"Thesis v\\\") else None\n    if vs in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"):\n        target_rows += 1\n        live_targets += int(\\\":\\\" not in digest)\n    if vs not in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v8\\\") or vs in seen:\n        continue\n    rebuilt=model.build_request(cfg.rejudging,request[\\\"messages\\\"][0][\\\"content\\\"],user,request[\\\"response_format\\\"][\\\"json_schema\\\"][\\\"schema\\\"],\\\"judgement\\\",cfg.provider)\n    seen[vs]=(cid,model.request_identity(rebuilt)[1]==digest)\nprint(\\\"First stored judge request rederived exactly:\\\",seen,\\\"target rows:\\\",target_rows,\\\"initially lookup-eligible:\\\",live_targets)'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
